@startuml player_state_machine
' Super Mario Plus - player behaviour transitions
' Verified against the source tree at commit b378acb.
' Matches: include/entity/Player/PlayerStates.h and src/entity/Player/Player*State.cpp

title Player State Machine — ten behaviours

[*] --> Idle

Idle  --> Run    : move pressed
Run   --> Idle   : movement stopped
Idle  --> Jump   : jump pressed
Run   --> Jump   : jump pressed
Jump  --> Fall   : upward velocity spent
Fall  --> Idle   : landed
Fall  --> Run    : landed while moving
Idle  --> Crouch : crouch pressed
Crouch --> Idle  : crouch released
Crouch --> Fall  : dropped through a one-way platform

Idle  --> Skill  : attack or skill pressed
Run   --> Skill  : attack or skill pressed
Jump  --> Skill  : aerial attack
Crouch --> Skill : crouching attack
Skill --> Skill  : combo continues to the next attack
Skill --> Idle   : animation finished

Idle  --> Climb  : on a ladder, climb pressed
Climb --> Fall   : left the ladder
Climb --> Jump   : jumped off

Idle  --> Swim   : entered water
Run   --> Swim   : entered water
Fall  --> Swim   : entered water
Swim  --> Fall   : left the water

Idle  --> Hurt   : took damage
Run   --> Hurt   : took damage
Jump  --> Hurt   : took damage
Skill --> Hurt   : took damage and canExit() allows it
Hurt  --> Idle   : recovery elapsed

Hurt  --> Die    : health reached zero
Skill --> Die    : health reached zero
Die   --> [*]    : respawn at the last checkpoint

note right of Skill
  canExit() returns false while an
  attack is in its active frames, so
  the attack cannot be interrupted
  part-way through.
end note

note bottom
  Base interface: PlayerState : IEntityState<Player>
    onEnter() / onExit() / update(dt)
    canExit()  -- interruption guard
    onMoveLeft / onMoveRight / onJump / onCrouch /
    onAttack / onClimb / onStop*  -- input handlers
end note

@enduml
